# Findings of the Trivy scan in the central CI pipeline that cannot be fixed here. Every entry expires on 2026-11-30: the
# build fails again then, so somebody has to look at the new upstream releases. Remove entries as upstream releases the
# fixes. (The Debian packages are clean, and the unused fixuid binary was removed from the image.) Findings that only
# show up for this image (JDK, Maven, Java extensions) are NOT ignored wholesale; each one is decided here.

# undici 7.29.1: HIGH. Bundled in the newest upstream base image (docker.io/codercom/code-server:4.144.0, released
# 2026-10-29, the newest tag): VS Code vendors it at that exact version in /usr/lib/code-server/lib/vscode/node_modules, so
# it cannot be fixed without replacing code-server's own dependency. The older findings of the base (shell-quote,
# basic-ftp, body-parser, follow-redirects, zod) are fixed in 4.144.0. Exposure: client-side fetch (extension gallery,
# updates); the IDE listens on 8080 behind the password and serves no requests through undici's server code.
# installed -> fixed e.g. 7.29.1 -> 7.30.1, 8.12.2
CVE-2026-109383 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-109829 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-109869 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-87018 exp:2026-11-30

# guava 33.7.1-jre: HIGH, denial of service (fixed in 33.7.2). A library inside the Red Hat Java extension
# (redhat.java 1.58.0, the language server's plugins), pinned in the Dockerfile to a stable release. The only newer builds
# on Open VSX (2026-10-29) are the nightly 1.59.2026... versions, which this image deliberately does not use. The language
# server analyses the student's own project in the student's own workspace; it is not reachable from other users.
# Look for a stable redhat.java release with guava >= 33.7.2.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-11-30
